    {
      "id": "jacobian",
      "name": "jacobian",
      "public": true,
      "semantic": "NONE",
      "uses": [
        {
          "target": "ARTICULATION",
          "description": "dense Jacobian",
          "dtype": "f32",
          "frame": "not_applicable",
          "units": "jacobian",
          "writability": "READ_ONLY",
          "read": {
            "layout": {
              "kind": "cohort",
              "lanes": 1,
              "shape": [
                "objects",
                "jacobian_rows",
                "jacobian_cols"
              ]
            },
            "conditions": [
              "session",
              "directgpu_warmup"
            ]
          },
          "write": false,
          "notes": "One group per structural cohort. M = numDofs + (fixedBase ? 0 : 6). Each row's dimensions are tensor axes, row-major, with lanes 1. Angular generalized coordinates are radians. centroidalMomentum is floating-base only; its last column is bias. Generalized joint coordinates follow the authored body relationship: sign +1 when body0 is the articulation parent and -1 when body1 is the parent. With S_dof containing those signs and T=S_dof for a fixed base or T=diag(I6,S_dof) for a floating base, the returned quantities are J=J_physx*T, M=T*M_physx*T, c=T*c_physx, g=T*g_physx, and [A|b]=[A_physx*T|b_physx]. Prismatic and floating-translation coordinates retain their linear units; angular coordinates receive no degree conversion."
        }
      ]
    },
